Technology Selection Depends on Process Chemistry

Semiconductor abatement solutions may use thermal, combustion-based, wet-treatment, plasma-assisted or other approaches depending on the exhaust stream. Some installations combine multiple treatment stages to address different chemical species.

No single technology is suitable for every application. Equipment selection must account for gas composition, treatment efficiency, secondary waste generation, water and power consumption, footprint, maintenance access and integration with facility controls.

The growing complexity of semiconductor manufacturing makes process-specific engineering and monitoring increasingly important.

